.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Functions for working with Windows Event Log (WEL) targets\&. 

WEL targets submit events using ReportEvent to a Windows system\&. By default, the category, message id, and type will use values based on the severity and facility of the logged event for messages included in Stumpless itself\&. If you need to use your own message files, use the functions in \fBstumpless/config/wel_supported\&.h\fP to specifically set these values\&. The formatted syslog message is included as the event binary data\&.
.PP
Note that if the event source is not installed the Event Viewer will not be able to display the messages or category text for received events\&. If you'd like to use the default messages included in Stumpless, use the stumpless_add_default_wel_event_source function to install it on the calling system\&.
.PP
This header will not be available in builds where Windows Event Log targets are not supported\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP Logging to WEL targets is thread safe by virtue of using the \fCReportEvent\fP function which is thread-safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP Logging to WEL targets is not signal safe, as a non-reentrant lock is used to coordinate the read of the entry's WEL data with other potential accesses\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP Logging to WEL targets is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock used for entry's WEL data may not be completed\&. 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void stumpless_close_wel_target (struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target)"

.PP
Closes a Windows Event Log target\&. In addition to closing the target, this function also destroys all memory allocated for the target, including the target struct itself\&.
.PP
If there is a problem while closing the target, then an error code will be set appropriately, the target will NOT be closed, and no memory will be released\&. To avoid a memory leak, check for errors using \fCstumpless_has_error\fP and resolve any errors that arise before calling this function again\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Unsafe\fP This function is not thread safe as it destroys resources that other threads would use if they tried to reference this target\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the destruction of a lock that may be in use as well as the use of the memory deallocation function to release memory\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the cleanup of the lock may not be completed, and the memory deallocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The Windows Event Log target to close\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_local_wel_target (const char * name)"

.PP
Opens a Windows Event Log target on the local machine\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that name is not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP The name of the target to open\&. This should match the name of the Windows Event Source that the logs will be added to\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * stumpless_open_remote_wel_target (const char * server, const char * name)"

.PP
Opens a Windows Event Log target on a remote machine\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:server race:name\fP This function is thread safe, of course assuming that server and name are not modified by any other threads during execution\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers due to the use of memory allocation functions\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe heap\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, as the memory allocation function may not be AC-Safe itself\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIserver\fP The remote server to log to\&. This should use the Universal Naming Convention (UNC) of the remote end\&. If this parameter is set to NULL, then the local machine is used\&. This is equivalent to a call to \fBstumpless_open_local_wel_target()\fP\&.
.br
\fIname\fP The name of the target to open\&. This should match the name of the Windows Event Source that the logs will be added to\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opened target if no error is encountered\&. In the event of an error, NULL is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. 
.RE
.PP

